  "pedal": "Boss DD-8 Digital Delay — focused reamp: guitar excerpts chosen for the repeats (mono: Output A)",
  "comment": "Excerpts of the guitar DI dataset (captures/di/) through the five modes NAM-X models. The stabs (five short chords, each followed by nearly two seconds of silence) are what a delay shows itself on: every repeat sounds alone in the gap, so its level, its tone and its time are read one by one, on guitar. Standard gets the full set: the stabs at full level and at -12 dB (the input clip: what doesn't scale with the level), the same take twice (the pedal against itself), the lead excerpt held out of any fit, Time at 9:00 and 3:00, Level at 9:00 and 5:00, Feedback at 3:00 (many repeats: how each one changes). Analog repeats the Feedback 3:00 take (its repeats darken one by one); Tape, Warm and Mod get the stabs, Mod also the strummed chords (sustained: its sweep). OUTPUT A to input 2, nothing in OUTPUT B; the pedal on its adapter. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise; 9:00 and 3:00 pointer horizontal. Each step turns one or two knobs.",
